    "body": "## Summary\nAdd visual show/hide password controls to all password fields so users can verify what they typed before submitting.\n\n## Motivation\nUsers can currently mistype passwords in masked fields and only discover the problem later when login fails. The existing password confirmation validation catches mismatches on setup flows, but it does not help when both fields contain the same unintended value or when a login password is mistyped.\n\n## Scope\n- Add an eye/show-hide toggle to the claim account password field.\n- Add the same toggle to the claim account password confirmation field.\n- Add the same toggle to reset-password fields.\n- Add the same toggle to login password fields.\n- Cover other user-facing password inputs if present, including registration and password-change forms.\n- Preserve existing minimum-length and password-match validation.\n- Keep the control accessible with clear labels such as \"Show password\" and \"Hide password\".\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- Users can toggle every user-facing password field between hidden and visible text.\n- Toggling visibility does not change the typed password value.\n- Password mismatch and minimum-length validation still work where applicable.\n- The UI works on mobile and desktop.",
