    "body": "### Summary\n\nImplement session detection for `GET /connect/*nostrconnect` (`connect_get` in\n  `api/src/api/http/oauth.rs`) so the nostr-login connect entry page can tell whether the\n  browser already has a valid Keycast UCAN session (`keycast_session` cookie), instead of\n  always treating the user as logged out.\n\n### Problem or Opportunity\n\nThe nostr-connect popup flow always shows the generic auth UI because `connect_get` never\n   reads or validates the session cookie. Users who are already signed into Keycast on that\n   origin still get a redundant login-style experience. Other OAuth/HTML paths\n  (`authorize_get`, `auth_status`) already validate the cookie against the tenant and\n  optionally resolve account/email for display and stale-cookie handling.\n\n### Proposed Approach\n\n- Extend `connect_get` with the same inputs used elsewhere: `TenantExtractor`,\n  `HeaderMap`, and `State<AuthState>` (pool access).\n- Reuse the existing cookie → UCAN validation pipeline already used in `oauth.rs`:\n    - `super::auth::extract_ucan_from_cookie(&headers)`\n    - `crate::ucan_auth::validate_ucan_token(&format!(\"Bearer {}\", token),\n  tenant_id).await`\n- Optionally mirror `authorize_get` behavior: resolve user via\n  `UserRepository::get_account_status`, clear stale cookies when the pubkey has no tenant\n  user row (unless you intentionally treat non-DB identities like NIP-07 admins the same as\n   `auth_status`).\n- Decide product behavior once `authenticated` is known (e.g. show “Signed in as …” /\n  shortened flow / alignment with `POST /oauth/connect`). This issue can scope “detect +\n  surface in HTML” or split UX into a follow-up if preferred.\n\n### Alternatives Considered\n\n  - Rely only on client-side `GET /oauth/auth-status` from the popup (extra round-trip;\n  duplicates logic unless server stays dumb).\n  - Pass UCAN in URL for GET (generally discouraged for tokens).\n\n### Mockups, Logs, or References\n\n  - TODO comment in `api/src/api/http/oauth.rs` above `connect_get` HTML assembly \nhttps://github.com/divinevideo/keycast/blob/6b05d9ecdefd21043a4a5cf7389cb339c32b56e5/api/src/api/http/oauth.rs#L3512\n  - Reference implementations: `auth_status`, `authorize_get`; tenant\n  resolution via `TenantExtractor` (`api/src/api/tenant.rs`).\n  - Route registration: `api/src/api/http/routes.rs`.",
